  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from OCR of scanned AK Butorphanol Tartrate Nasal Spray (Stadol) Criteria Version 2; Last updated 06/24/09. Source PDF is image-only (HP MFP); text recovered via tesseract 2026-09-27.",
    "effective_date uses Last updated 2009-06-24 (replaces ingestion stub 2009-01-01).",
    "Product: nasal spray 10 mg/mL in 2.5 mL vials. FDA indication (notes only): management of pain when use of an opioid analgesic is appropriate.",
    "Approval criteria 1–2 always apply on the standard path; criterion 3 (cannot use combo opioid+APAP/ASA/IBU) OR criterion 4 (migraine with prophylaxis and triptans unless contraindicated) are alternate branches.",
    "Pharmacy may override PA for hospice, cancer, or LTC.",
    "Authorization (notes only): up to 3 months. Dispensing limit (notes only): 2 units (5 mL) per month.",
    "Additional information (notes only): not recommended in opioid-dependent patients; may precipitate withdrawal; caution after recent repeated narcotic doses."
